{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Lean and ill-favored of form exceedingly and thin of flesh.</b> And the lean cows, and the seven lean cows, and the seven lean ears — in all four of them the word is spelled with resh-yod in the first instance and resh-yod in the latter instance with tsere. Pharaoh's dream was doubled for the honor of Joseph."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {0 "The Hebrew note contrasts two spellings of the word for 'lean'; both instances are spelled with resh-yod but with different vowel pointing (the first apparently with a different vocalization, the latter with tsere). The technical spelling note is rendered literally as the distinction does not map cleanly to English orthography."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:14.142560913Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}